" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -704 1542 898\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(751,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D444\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D444\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> subtends an angle <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.381ex\" height=\"1.649ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -707 1936.6 729\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1533,393.1) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> at the center <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.726ex\" height=\"1.643ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -704 763 726\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> of the spherical shell, as shown in the figure. The permittivity of free space is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.126ex\" height=\"1.596ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -540 1381.6 705.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2208\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2208\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(700,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1103.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"2E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> Which of the following statement is (are) true? \n<br><br><img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/jXZLOn8ALRXJgzNBB/a9NUE4LA6IIPbrHCw7BqyR4y63BrE/w2MMKo3wyQ8j9W17l0ZT69/image.png\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2018 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Electrostatics Question 52 English\">  ","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"The electric flux through the shell is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.566ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"9.725ex\" height=\"2.713ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -949 4298.6 1199\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msqrt\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0,89)\"><use data-c=\"221A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-221A\"></use></g><g transform=\"translate(853,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"500\" height=\"60\" x=\"853\" y