width=\"24.331ex\" height=\"2.713ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -949 10754.2 1199\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D719\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D719\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(873.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(1929.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(479,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D452\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D452\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(466,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1066,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D450\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D450\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3518.5,0)\"><use data-c=\"2F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(4018.5,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2208\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2208\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(700,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(5399.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msqrt\" transform=\"translate(6455.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0,89)\"><use data-c=\"221A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-221A\"></use></g><g transform=\"translate(853,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"500\" height=\"60\" x=\"853\" y=\"829\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(7808.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D445\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D445\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(8567.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D706\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D706\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(9150.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"2F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(9650.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2208\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2208\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(700,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>.</p>\n<p>The electric field at a point due to the infinitely long line charge is radial i.e., perpendicular to the line PQ. The non-conducting spherical shell does not affect or alter the electric field. Thus, electric field at a point lying on the surface of the shell is perpendicular to the z-axis i.e., its z component is zero. The figure shows electric field on the surface of the shell for a positive line charge. Note that the magnitude of electric field is inversely proportional to the distance of the point from the line charge.</p>","qKey":"SgmLRpZk1yddkopo","paperKey":"jee-advanced-2018-paper-2-offline","exam":"jee-advanced"}]}